/T (2. Edge Computing: The "Local" Brain - one of the biggest hurdles for tech was the "delay" caused by sending data to a server and back. Today, Physical AI processes information "at the edge" - right inside the device. This allows for split-second decision-making, which is essential for the safety of autonomous community shuttles and sidewalk delivery bots navigating our busy streets. )
/E (2. Edge Computing: The "Local" Brain - one of the biggest hurdles for tech was the "delay" caused by sending data to a server and back. Today, Physical AI processes information "at the edge" - right inside the device. This allows for split-second decision-making, which is essential for the safety of autonomous community shuttles and sidewalk delivery bots navigating our busy streets. )
